{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs",
  "item": "impl[CachedParse/SourceProvider]/fn[read]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This required SourceProvider callback is an error guard: the fixture\n supplies cached snapshots by overriding parse. Structural search must\n use those snapshots without refetching. Calling read would fail the\n contract tested below; primitive reads are exercised by other providers."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/sources/tests.rs` `impl[CachedParse/SourceProvider]/fn[read]` is valid.\n\n- **Form:** It is a fenced citation with commentary placed directly on an explicit function with a body. That is the form the built-in allows for a function-level coverage exception.\n- **Substantive reason:** The commentary says `read` is a required trait callback that acts as an error guard. The fixture overrides `parse` to supply cached snapshots, and structural search must not refetch. If `read` were called, the contract would fail. This explains why zero execution is acceptable, and difficulty is not the reason given.\n- **Agreement with source:**\n  - The `read` body only returns `SourceError::Invalid(\"cached parser must not refetch\")`.\n  - The same impl overrides `parse` with a fixed `fn cached() { call(); }` snapshot and counts parses in `parses`.\n  - The default `defaults::search_structure` in `sources.rs` carries the comment \"The provider's override supplies the parse and its source snapshot\". It goes through `provider.parse`, not `read`, so the guard should not run.\n  - The test `structural_search_uses_overridden_parses_their_snapshot_and_requested_scope` exercises that path.\n- **Other providers:** The claim that primitive reads are exercised elsewhere holds. Tests such as `defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot` and `local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root` call `read` on other providers.\n- **Redundancy:** The item has no other references to the same target, so the citation is not redundant.",
